    {
        "content": "<p>I believe <code>Iter.enumerate</code> would be more conventional with the exception of Scala/Elixir/Kotlin/Ruby</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Language</th>\n<th>Idiom / API</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Python</strong></td>\n<td><code>enumerate(xs)</code></td>\n<td><code>(index, value)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Rust</strong></td>\n<td><code>xs.iter().enumerate()</code></td>\n<td><code>(index, value)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Swift</strong></td>\n<td><code>xs.enumerated()</code></td>\n<td><code>(offset, element)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>C# / LINQ</strong></td>\n<td><code>xs.Select((x, i) =&gt; ...)</code></td>\n<td>selector receives value + index</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>JavaScript</strong></td>\n<td><code>xs.entries()</code></td>\n<td><code>[index, value]</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Go</strong></td>\n<td><code>for i, x := range xs</code></td>\n<td>index + value, but language syntax</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>C++ ranges</strong></td>\n<td><code>views::enumerate</code> <strong>C++23</strong></td>\n<td>tuple-like <code>(index, value)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Haskell</strong></td>\n<td><code>zip [0..] xs</code></td>\n<td><code>(index, value)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Scala</strong></td>\n<td><code>xs.zipWithIndex</code></td>\n<td><code>(value, index)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Elixir</strong></td>\n<td><code>Enum.with_index(xs)</code></td>\n<td><code>{value, index}</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Kotlin</strong></td>\n<td><code>xs.withIndex()</code></td>\n<td><code>IndexedValue(index, value)</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ruby</strong></td>\n<td><code>xs.each_with_index</code></td>\n<td>value + index</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Dart</strong></td>\n<td>no core <code>enumerate</code>; commonly indexed extensions/packages</td>\n<td>varies</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Julia</strong></td>\n<td><code>enumerate(xs)</code></td>\n<td><code>(index, value)</code>, <strong>1-based</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Zig</strong></td>\n<td>typically <code>for (xs, 0..) \\|x, i\\|</code></td>\n<td>language syntax</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Gleam</strong></td>\n<td><code>list.index_map</code> / iterator equivalents depending on abstraction</td>\n<td>index supplied to function</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
        "id": 620780075,
        "sender_full_name": "Romain Lepert",
        "timestamp": 1788292968
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Coming from Python, I like <code>enumerate</code>, but since we have <code>List.map_with_index</code>, <code>List.fold_with_index</code>, and several <code>with_...</code> functions, I think I prefer <code>with_index</code> for consistency. Also, <code>enumerate</code> is only used in one more language than <code>with_index</code>.</p>",
        "id": 620799337,
        "sender_full_name": "Aurélien Geron",
        "timestamp": 1788297706
    }
]